# Vendored C sources — fetched on demand by scripts/fetch-vendor-sqlite3.sh
# instead of committed to the repo. The amalgamation is ~10 MB of binary-like
# data that bloats git clones and has no diffable content (only version
# bumps). For non-Linux targets (Windows, macOS, cross-compile from Linux),
# the build.zig references vendor/sqlite3/sqlite3.c directly — the fetch
# script restores it on demand before the first zig build call.
#
# To regenerate after bumping SQLite: delete vendor/sqlite3/ and re-run
# `scripts/fetch-vendor-sqlite3.sh`.
/vendor/

# Test artifacts (created by zig build test runs)
test_logger_*.log
test_logger_nested_dir/
test_diff_view_*.txt
test_*.log

# Functional test venv + cache (created by `zig build functional-test`)
.venv-func/
.pytest_cache/
